# GitHub reads this file and puts a "Cite this repository" button on the
# repository page, which produces the APA and BibTeX forms automatically.
cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Superpoint Graph Viewer: an interactive nested acyclic graph of topographic change on the Isar"
message: "If you use this viewer or the partition it draws, please cite the thesis it accompanies."
type: software
repository-code: "https://github.com/USER/isar-superpoint-viewer"
url: "https://USER.github.io/isar-superpoint-viewer/"
authors:
  - family-names: Wong
    given-names: "Ching Yeung"
    affiliation: "Technical University of Munich"
license:
  - MIT          # the viewer code
  - CC-BY-4.0    # everything under data/
keywords:
  - point cloud
  - change detection
  - superpoint graph
  - M3C2
  - nested acyclic graph
  - fluvial geomorphology
  - web cartography
abstract: >-
  A static, dependency-free web viewer for the four-level hierarchical
  partition used in an MSc Cartography thesis on topographic change
  segmentation. It draws 150,000 voxels and 10,061 first-level superpoints
  from a nested acyclic graph, with the M3C2 distance, the four change-tensor
  components, the label purity and the purity gate available as colour, and
  the digitised water's edge of both survey epochs available as an overlay.

references:
  - type: thesis
    title: "Topographic Change Segmentation from Multi-Temporal Point Clouds using Superpoint Graphs"
    thesis-type: "MSc thesis"
    authors:
      - family-names: Wong
        given-names: "Ching Yeung"
    institution:
      name: "Technical University of Munich"
    year: 2026
    month: 9
